{% doc %}
  @description Wraps POST /v4/records/{recordId}/documents (Accela "Create Record Documents").

    Accela requires multipart/form-data with two parts: `uploadedFile`
    (the binary) and `fileInfo` (a JSON string array of metadata).

    *** VERIFY BEFORE PRODUCTION USE ***
    platformOS API Call Notifications support a `post_multipart` request
    type, but the exact Liquid syntax for attaching a raw file part inside
    the notification template is not clearly documented. The current
    implementation in public/api_calls/accela_post_multipart.liquid is a
    best-effort scaffold - confirm against your platformOS instance/support
    how binary file uploads should be represented in an API Call
    Notification body (likely needs the file made available via a prior
    file-upload mutation and referenced by URL/id rather than inlined).

    MULTIPART requests are only retried when `file_object_id`/
    `file_object_property` are given alongside `with_retries` - file
    content otherwise can't be safely re-sent from a detached background
    job (see lib/accela_client/send.liquid).

    Follows the pos-module-core build/check/execute command pattern (see
    upload/{build,check}.liquid): build prepares the request URL and the
    `fileInfo` body, check validates required params, and this file
    executes the request itself once valid (rather than delegating to a
    separate execute.liquid).
  @param {string} record_id - Record id (required)
  @param {string} [file_field] - Raw file content or a reference to already-uploaded file data
  @param {string} file_name - Original file name, e.g. "site_plan.pdf"
  @param {string} content_type - MIME type, e.g. "application/pdf" (required)
  @param {string} [category] - must match a value from documents/categories
  @param {string} [description] - description string
  @param {object} [reference] - hash `{ "id", "table" }` forwarded to
    send.liquid - see send.liquid.
  @param {boolean} [with_retries] - default false. When true, retries a
    failed attempt in the background with increasing delay - see
    lib/accela_client/send.liquid. Only meaningful when
    `file_object_id`/`file_object_property` are also given (see below) -
    otherwise this MULTIPART request still can't be retried, since raw
    file bytes can't be carried through a background job.
  @param {string} [file_object_id] - optional, given together with
    file_object_property. Identify a platformOS generic_object record and
    the file property on it holding this upload's file content (already
    stored there by an earlier upload step), as an alternative to relying
    on `file_field`'s raw bytes surviving into a background retry.
    Forwarded to send.liquid as `metadata.file_object_id`/
    `metadata.file_object_property` - when both are present,
    send.liquid re-downloads the file fresh from that generic_object
    on every attempt (this call and any retries) instead of needing
    the file content itself carried down the retry chain. This is what
    makes `with_retries` viable for a MULTIPART upload - see
    lib/accela_client/send.liquid.
  @param {string} [file_object_property] - optional, given together with
    file_object_id. Identify a platformOS generic_object record and
    the file property on it holding this upload's file content (already
    stored there by an earlier upload step), as an alternative to relying
    on `file_field`'s raw bytes surviving into a background retry.
    Forwarded to send.liquid as `metadata.file_object_id`/
    `metadata.file_object_property` - when both are present,
    send.liquid re-downloads the file fresh from that generic_object
    on every attempt (this call and any retries) instead of needing
    the file content itself carried down the retry chain. This is what
    makes `with_retries` viable for a MULTIPART upload - see
    lib/accela_client/send.liquid.
  @example
    {% function result = 'modules/accela_construct/commands/records/documents/upload',
       record_id: record_id, file_field: file_content, file_name: 'site_plan.pdf',
       content_type: 'application/pdf', description: 'Site plan' %}
{% enddoc %}

{% liquid
  assign object = { "errors": {}, "valid": true, "record_id": record_id, "file_field": file_field, "file_name": file_name, "content_type": content_type, "category": category, "description": description }
  function object = 'modules/accela_construct/commands/records/documents/upload/build', object: object
  function object = 'modules/accela_construct/commands/records/documents/upload/check', object: object

  if object.valid
    assign metadata = { "file_object_id": file_object_id, "file_object_property": file_object_property }
    function result = 'modules/accela_construct/accela_client/send', method: 'MULTIPART', path: object.path, file_field: object.file_field, file_info: object.file_info, reference: reference, caller: 'modules/accela_construct/commands/records/documents/upload', with_retries: with_retries, metadata: metadata
  else
    function result = 'modules/accela_construct/accela_client/error_result', error: 'accela_validation_failed', errors: object.errors, caller: 'modules/accela_construct/commands/records/documents/upload'
  endif

  return result
%}
